---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Terminal from '../../../components/Terminal.astro';
import InstallCommand from '../../../components/InstallCommand.astro';
import DocsPagination from '../../../components/DocsPagination.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Getting started — Git Treeline"
  description="Install Git Treeline on macOS or Linux, configure your project, and run your first isolated Git worktree."
  canonical="https://git-treeline.dev/docs/getting-started/"
  activePage="getting-started"
>
  <div class="docs-guide pt-20 sm:pt-24 pb-16 sm:pb-20 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-0">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-sm text-muted mb-6">
      <a href="/docs/" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Docs</a>
      <span class="mx-1.5">/</span>
      <span class="text-white">Getting started</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-mono font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-4">Getting started</h1>
    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-muted max-w-2xl mb-4">
      Run a second branch without sharing the first branch's ports or database. Install the CLI, configure your existing project, then create a worktree.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-8">Verified against CLI v0.58.3. <a href="#upgrading" class="text-accent-light underline underline-offset-2">Upgrading an existing installation?</a></p>
    <p class="mb-8">
      You'll need <strong class="text-white">macOS or Linux, Git, and your project's runtimes and dependencies</strong>. For database cloning, prepare a PostgreSQL template database or SQLite file. Containers are optional.
    </p>

    <h2 id="install">1. Install the CLI</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">With Homebrew on macOS or Linux:</p>
    <InstallCommand />
    <details class="rounded-lg border border-surface-border px-4 py-3 mt-4 mb-8">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer text-accent-light">Go install or download a binary</summary>
      <div class="pt-4 space-y-4">
        <p>With Go 1.26 or later:</p>
        <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded bg-surface-raised p-3 text-sm"><code>go install github.com/git-treeline/cli/cmd/git-treeline@latest</code></pre>
        <p>Or download a binary from the <a href="https://github.com/git-treeline/cli/releases" class="text-accent-light underline underline-offset-2">releases page</a>.</p>
        <p>Homebrew installs both <code class="text-accent-light">git-treeline</code> and the <code class="text-accent-light">gtl</code> alias used below. Go install provides <code class="text-accent-light">git-treeline</code>; use that command in place of <code class="text-accent-light">gtl</code>. It also works as <code class="text-accent-light">git treeline</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <h2 id="configure">2. Configure your project</h2>
    <div class="mb-5">
      <Terminal>
        <pre class="text-sm sm:text-base"><code>cd ~/myapp
gtl install</code></pre>
      </Terminal>
    </div>
    <p class="mb-4">
      Treeline detects supported frameworks, creates <code class="text-accent-light">.treeline.yml</code> if needed, installs a Git hook, and allocates resources for the current checkout. Review the generated setup and start commands for your app.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-4">
      Local HTTPS is optional. Accepting the router setup requires administrator authorization to trust a local certificate and configure forwarding. Skip it to use <code class="text-accent-light">localhost</code>; you can run <code class="text-accent-light">gtl serve install</code> later.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-8">
      For an annotated config and framework-specific setup, follow the <a href="/use-cases/first-time-setup/" class="text-accent-light underline underline-offset-2">full setup walkthrough</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="create">3. Create and start a worktree</h2>
    <div class="mb-5">
      <Terminal>
        <pre class="text-sm sm:text-base"><code>gtl new feature-auth --start</code></pre>
      </Terminal>
    </div>
    <p class="mb-4">
      This creates the worktree, allocates its ports, writes its env file, runs your setup commands, and starts the configured server. If database cloning is configured, the worktree gets its own copy of the template. A named HTTPS URL requires the optional router.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-8">
      Open another terminal in the new worktree and run <code class="text-accent-light">gtl doctor</code> to check its configuration and runtime. To review a GitHub PR instead, use <code class="text-accent-light">gtl review 42 --start</code> from the main checkout; this requires the <a href="https://cli.github.com/" class="text-accent-light underline underline-offset-2">GitHub CLI</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="next">Choose what you need next</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3 mb-8">
      <li><a href="/docs/database/" class="text-accent-light underline underline-offset-2">Database isolation</a> — PostgreSQL cloning, SQLite copies, and template updates.</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/networking/" class="text-accent-light underline underline-offset-2">Networking</a> — local HTTPS names, stable callback ports, and public tunnels.</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/lifecycle/" class="text-accent-light underline underline-offset-2">Lifecycle</a> — switch branches, start and stop servers, and release resources.</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/agents/" class="text-accent-light underline underline-offset-2">AI agents</a> — give agents access to real allocations and server controls.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="upgrading">Upgrading to v0.58.3</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      Run <code class="text-accent-light">gtl update</code>, then <code class="text-accent-light">gtl version</code> to confirm the installed version.
      See the <a href="https://github.com/git-treeline/cli/releases/tag/v0.58.3" class="text-accent-light underline underline-offset-2">release notes</a> for all changes.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-4">
      Template updates now run in a temporary detached checkout, leaving your primary checkout unchanged. They require Git 2.29 or later and an explicit primary database mapping in <code class="text-accent-light">env</code>. Review the <a href="/docs/database/#updating-the-template" class="text-accent-light underline underline-offset-2">template update requirements</a> before using <code class="text-accent-light">database.sync_on_create</code> or <code class="text-accent-light">gtl db template update</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-10">
      Coming from v0.58.0 or earlier? Stop each older supervisor with <code class="text-accent-light">gtl stop --kill</code> from the same directory path used to launch it (including any symlink alias), then run <code class="text-accent-light">gtl start</code>. Ctrl+C in its original terminal also works.
    </p>
    <DocsPagination next={{ href: '/docs/lifecycle/', label: 'Lifecycle' }} />
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
